{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like","id":656711,"title":"What would a Victorious garou nation look like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-08T10:50:31-07:00","id":656711,"title":"What would a Victorious garou nation look like?","content":"Hard to imagine an unqualified Victory for the Garou nation not involving a renewel of the impergium. or something equally Drastic... as its only &quot;Unqualified&quot; IF pentex is utterly ANNIHILATED from existence, along with the dancers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:42:51-07:00","id":656866,"title":"","content":"The distant future epilogue for Final Fantasy 7 comes to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T14:41:28-07:00","id":656935,"title":"","content":"If Werewolves won, there would be a huge fight as to what happens next with some like the Glasswalkers wanting to keep things as they are, and some like Red Talons wanting to genocide humanity. <br /> <br /> I imagine that ultimately there would be a compromise, and they would decide that humans could be left alive, but modern Weaver-technology has to go. I just can't see Werewolves agreeing to keep humanity and the world &quot;as is.&quot; Most likely there would be an attempt to move humanity back to a pre-industrial state, something akin to Medieval Europe, Tokugawa Japan, etc, with humans being openly ruled and controlled by Werewolves. <br /> <br /> There might be limited technological enclaves in certain places under the control of Glasswalkers, Shadowlords, Children of Gaia, etc, <br /> <br /> It would amount to a neo-Impergium, though probably not <i>quite</i> as bad as the original, which was beyond nightmarish. Still, I expect quite a few places would end up with results very similar to Cambodia's Khmer Rouge, who killed anyone that was educated, literate and use things like glasses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T04:54:57-07:00","id":657650,"title":"","content":"Ohh what a terrifying idea. The Garou win and possibly have the chance to rule?!<br /> <br /> Oh my<br /> <br /> well...if it was me I would say the win also came a heavy cost. A huge sacrifice on behalf of the Garou as a nation.<br /> <br /> I would go with the story of an awesome pack returning from an umbral quest with the rite used by the Croatan Tribe to banish the Eater of Souls from when it last tried to step into the realm.<br /> <br /> Then I'd have some one come up with a crazy plan to do it again. Three times. One for each head of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> For the Beast of War I'd have a lot of challenges go down and tribal conflict to prove which tribe should have the honor and glory of doing so. Eventually, the Get of Fenris claim the place.<br /> <br /> With the Eater of Souls, there is much debating and consideration. Eventually the Children of Gaia with Pegasus take the responsibility.<br /> <br /> and finally with the Eater of Souls...the Silver Fangs. In recognition of the failures to stop the evil from eating away at everything (in their leadership in the nation, as a tribe, as rulers ordained by gaia) Take the place as sacrifice so gaia and the Garou (their subjects obviously) may go on. (Big grins on the shadow lord faces!)<br /> <br /> They do it. All three Tribes take to their original homelands and each and everyone of them gives everything they have.<br /> <br /> It works. The Triatic wyrm is weakened and pushed back to the hells they came from. But at a terrible cost.<br /> <br /> The Garou are now without their leaders, without their healers and without the martial prowess of the Get. (Plus the Fianna have to always sing of the Gets great sacrifice...ha!)<br /> <br /> What do they do now? Who is in charge? Who will fullfill the roles now a void left in the abscence of thesacrificed tribes?<br /> <br /> What of the wyld and the weaver? Who shall lead? Gaia!!.. what do you want of us!!! They howl, quest, and pray for the answers.<br /> <br /> That would be where I would start it with the players.The worId in ruins, but free (for now) of the wyrm. The Garou nation in chaos and remorse deep in uncertainty.<br /> <br /> Then well...I'd bring in a new changing breed(or old depending if you believe that one shadow lord). WereFalcons. Who soar the sky under Falcons banner, who's gifts of battle and healing reflect those who once sacrificed themselves under the garou banner.<br /> <br /> and behind them...the rest of the changing breeds.<br /> <br /> Gaia has answered.<br /> <br /> This time, they must do it...together. there will not be another chance.<br /> <br /> add the world still needs cleansing. That pockets of blights and pollution still breed banes and spew corruption, that the Weaver is still taking and staticically enforcing its hold over new lands, that tbe Wyld is rattling at its cage and bursting fourth new things in the wake of the averted apocalypse.<br /> <br /> and that the shadow lords want the leadership over all now.<br /> that the red talons have the rite too and wonder if it can be used against the Weaver.<br /> That surviving black spirals no longer know what yo do.<br /> Pentex is free to do what it wants<br /> the wars and old battles still rage. Cutting off the heads of the hydra didnt magically make all them stop.<br /> oh no. There's still more to do.<br /> Plus, we can never forget...not this time.<br /> <br /> That would be me and my brain. The garou and fera all coming together to decide who will rule, who will follow, and who will rise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:43:12-07:00","id":657921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=657650#post657650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ohh what a terrifying idea. The Garou win and possibly have the chance to rule?!<br /> <br /> Oh my<br /> <br /> well...if it was me I would say the win also came a heavy cost. A huge sacrifice on behalf of the Garou as a nation.<br /> <br /> I would go with the story of an awesome pack returning from an umbral quest with the rite used by the Croatan Tribe to banish the Eater of Souls from when it last tried to step into the realm.<br /> <br /> Then I'd have some one come up with a crazy plan to do it again. Three times. One for each head of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was specifically to stop it from getting into the physical world. At present, none of the Triatic Wyrms are actually breaking through, and even banishing them in this manner doesn't do a job that could be called &quot;victorious&quot;, even if it's all three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:51:55-07:00","id":657932,"title":"","content":"Golden rule <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:54:49-07:00","id":657937,"title":"","content":"Or whatever is needed to fit. Like.. &quot;it turns out if you perform it against all three at the same time it has an even greater affect.&quot; <br /> <br /> Or a clever bunch of Theurges and Spirits come up with a way.<br /> <br /> you know, how ever an imagination conjours an answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T08:52:24-07:00","id":659415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=656935#post656935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Werewolves won, there would be a huge fight as to what happens next with some like the Glasswalkers wanting to keep things as they are, and some like Red Talons wanting to genocide humanity. <br /> <br /> I imagine that ultimately there would be a compromise, and they would decide that humans could be left alive, but modern Weaver-technology has to go. I just can't see Werewolves agreeing to keep humanity and the world &amp;quot;as is.&amp;quot; Most likely there would be an attempt to move humanity back to a pre-industrial state, something akin to Medieval Europe, Tokugawa Japan, etc, with humans being openly ruled and controlled by Werewolves. <br /> <br /> There might be limited technological enclaves in certain places under the control of Glasswalkers, Shadowlords, Children of Gaia, etc, <br /> <br /> It would amount to a neo-Impergium, though probably not <i>quite</i> as bad as the original, which was beyond nightmarish. Still, I expect quite a few places would end up with results very similar to Cambodia's Khmer Rouge, who killed anyone that was educated, literate and use things like glasses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked your post. The only thing I find strange is that 'not as bad'. Can you imagine the brutality of the attack needed to destroy the human industry and their capability to rebuild it? I think that would need a much worse Impergium that simply stopping the humans to achieve a Neolithic state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3673-mu_","name":"Mu_","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3673_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T09:52:13-07:00","id":659462,"title":"","content":"I just mean in the general long-term - that is, for people who were born and raised in this neo-Impergium, life would probably be better for them than it would have been during the original Impergium.<br /> <br /> In this scenario I suggested, you would still have humans living in villages and towns, you'd probably have metal working to a degree, you'd have farming and some level of book knowledge. If you're one of the truly lucky ones that end up living in a Glasswalker enclave, there might not even be anything too different from life before the Apocalypse and afterwards. Regardless, the average quality of life for humans would be rather higher than it was for the humans who were living during the original Imergium.<br /> <br /> Of course for the people living in the modern society, and find themselves being culled to create this neo-Impergium, things are going to be pretty terrible and being told, &quot;Well you guys are better off now than you were during the original Impergium&quot; would be a small consolation. Ultimately though it all depends on how the Apocalypse itself played out.<br /> <br /> A near victory by the Wyrm, in which 90% of the population dies, the survivors realize that they are being protected by werewolves, and then come to understand the dangers of technology and choose to join the werewolves in &quot;dialing back the clock&quot;... well, life would be a bit worse for the survivors, but it wouldn't necessarily be because of the werewolves and certainly the &quot;human/werewolf&quot; relationship would be a lot better than it was during the original Impergium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T10:23:30-07:00","id":659502,"title":"","content":"hmmmn thats interesting Anubis kind of like the &quot;Wyld World&quot;<br /> <br /> another idea? Is come in and Mandate, population Quotas, enforcing them through threats of death, BEFORE Actualy enforcing them with Death.<br /> <br /> In the Nagah breed book its suggested as an ideal world, a world, with citys, medicine, and Art, but not as many humans, choking the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:54:23-07:00","id":659981,"title":"","content":"Honestly, it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Actually winning against Pentex and the BSD's is but a tip of the iceberg. Either of those feats would decimate the Garou and leave them quite worse for wear and still leave them fighting the Wyrm which has a million tendrils into the world beyond the most obvious ones - from Banes to random Fomori and Fomori families. It's such a task that after it happens there isn't really any more Werewolf the Apocalypse. What would be left of the Garou would be unrecognizeable and everything to follow would stem from the facts of who survived and what was actually sacrificed to achieve it.<br /> <br /> What would happen in the practical impossibility where the Garou Nation as a whole survived all of that... well most likely a short period of peace before heavy duty politics started on how to actually save Gaia and control the excesses of humanity. Doing such a blow would most likely strengthen the Weaver, hopefully giving the Garou a common threat to deal with rather then the politics and chaos that would ensue from them trying to fix the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T13:21:23-07:00","id":661008,"title":"","content":"Assuming a miraculously successful war that left the Garou in charge and in which they didn't suffer severe casualties?<br /> <br /> Humans get genocided down to less than a billion. There's peace until werewolves numbers get high enough, then they start killing each other. Inter-tribal packs become a thing of the past as the tribes start fighting amongst each other. The Wyrn is no longer a problem, but as mentioned in the Wild West book, the Wild is actually a threat now, with numerous Wyld spirits growing out of control in a now thin gauntlet. Wyrn spirits now actually have to be protected, because they start failing in their proper duty of recycling rot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T13:36:07-07:00","id":661039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=661008#post661008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming a miraculously successful war that left the Garou in charge and in which they didn't suffer severe casualties?<br /> <br /> Humans get genocided down to less than a billion.</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably would have suffered huge casualties at least on that order over the course of the Garou seizing victory. honestly. With all of the fights in the Umbra, the spillover into the physical realm would be substantial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's peace until werewolves numbers get high enough, then they start killing each other. Inter-tribal packs become a thing of the past as the tribes start fighting amongst each other. The Wyrn is no longer a problem, but as mentioned in the Wild West book, the Wild is actually a threat now, with numerous Wyld spirits growing out of control in a now thin gauntlet. Wyrn spirits now actually have to be protected, because they start failing in their proper duty of recycling rot. </div> </div> </div>Wyld spirits are already a threat. Thresholds and Abcesses aren't tolerated on caerns, as they will cause a caern to become warped. The Wyld is a roving disaster that simply happens to have been pushed more into the Umbra than other manifestations of the Triat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T02:15:26-07:00","id":661679,"title":"","content":"IMO it would probably look like the Apocalypse. The only thing keeping these Rage-filled monsters from turning on each other is all the enemies taking priority. Eliminate all those and the last great Garou civil war breaks out as tribe destroys tribe for supremacy.<br /> <br /> Eventually one tribe is left standing, and it cannibalises itself as sept turns on sept and pack turns on pack to decide who rules the tribe. When the last pack is all that remains, the members turn on each other to be alpha. <br /> <br /> Eventually the Garou are no more, and Gaia shudders and dies, as her warriors defeated everything, killed all enemies, and when they destroyed their enemies they went looking for more, and they found enemies where they'd previously seen none.<br /> <br /> When all you have is a hammer, you can only hit things. The Garou were Gaia's greatest warriors, her strongest children, her greatest triumph - and her ultimate doom. This was fated the moment she birthed the first Garou cub.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T02:27:42-07:00","id":661686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=661679#post661679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO it would probably look like the Apocalypse. The only thing keeping these Rage-filled monsters from turning on each other is all the enemies taking priority. Eliminate all those and the last great Garou civil war breaks out as tribe destroys tribe for supremacy.<br /> <br /> Eventually one tribe is left standing, and it cannibalises itself as sept turns on sept and pack turns on pack to decide who rules the tribe. When the last pack is all that remains, the members turn on each other to be alpha.<br /> <br /> Eventually the Garou are no more, and Gaia shudders and dies, as her warriors defeated everything, killed all enemies, and when they destroyed their enemies they went looking for more, and they found enemies where they'd previously seen none.<br /> <br /> When all you have is a hammer, you can only hit things. The Garou were Gaia's greatest warriors, her strongest children, her greatest triumph - and her ultimate doom. This was fated the moment she birthed the first Garou cub.</div> </div> </div> </div>... that's a bleak vision of Garou. They are not that bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T02:45:43-07:00","id":661708,"title":"","content":"...and so very very World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I like it as a bleak view forseen that only adds to the Harano of those who have tried so hard, given so much and yet still cant control or undo centuries of distrust, hurt, dispair and philosophical differences between Gaias Garou.<br /> <br /> of course if you (anyone rather than someone specific) wanted a more positive tale to tell you could do something else. If it was me, I'd have the Changing Breeds all come together after the Apocalypse realising they are all on the brink of extinction if they dont.<br /> <br /> If you have players who cross the breeds you could have them all supporting each other and promote awareness of their roles and have each take them up unhindered in recognition if they dont stick to gaias mandates they could all fail.<br /> <br /> or if you wanted to create your own future of the Fera have them petition Gaia to give them new mandates and roles for the World's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T02:46:50-07:00","id":661709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=661679#post661679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO it would probably look like the Apocalypse. The only thing keeping these Rage-filled monsters from turning on each other is all the enemies taking priority. Eliminate all those and the last great Garou civil war breaks out as tribe destroys tribe for supremacy.<br /> <br /> Eventually one tribe is left standing, and it cannibalises itself as sept turns on sept and pack turns on pack to decide who rules the tribe. When the last pack is all that remains, the members turn on each other to be alpha.<br /> <br /> Eventually the Garou are no more, and Gaia shudders and dies, as her warriors defeated everything, killed all enemies, and when they destroyed their enemies they went looking for more, and they found enemies where they'd previously seen none.<br /> <br /> When all you have is a hammer, you can only hit things. The Garou were Gaia's greatest warriors, her strongest children, her greatest triumph - and her ultimate doom. This was fated the moment she birthed the first Garou cub.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Holy sh** are we having a bright day, Bunyip. xD<br /> <br /> I don't agree with you in the least. Yes, they are the warriors. But they are not possessed mindlessly by their task. Once they are finished with their purpose, they will be set to protect what is achieved. They are the NK lymphocytes, not the cancer. A body CAN and MUST have its defenses. My vision would be akin to AnubisXy's one. Neo-impergium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T04:45:13-07:00","id":661786,"title":"","content":"It's called 'Werewolf: the Apocalypse' and 'World of Darkness' for a reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T04:53:32-07:00","id":661789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=661709#post661709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree with you in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=661709#post661709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once they are finished with their purpose, they will be set to protect what is achieved.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they can't. They can try, but they'll end up destroying it. If they didn't have Rage, they would be able to. But they go have Rage. They will grow angry, furious beyond what humans can comprehend. They'll find irritation and insult in small things, because the big things that Rage is meant to be used for no longer exists. They'll frenzy, and destroy, and taste blood and flesh.<br /> <br /> They'll fulfil their purpose until the last Garou falls. No matter how hard they try, they can't help but to do otherwise. It's how Gaia designed them.<br /> <br /> They may have been intended to be an immune system, but Rage was their strength and their flaw, and they've long since become a cancer. Just ask the Fera, particularly the Grondr, or the Camaztotz. Ask the Bunyip, if you like. <br /> <br /> Part of the tragedy of the Garou is that increasingly more of them have realised this, and despite their best efforts they can't change who they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 09-12-2015, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T05:28:01-07:00","id":661812,"title":"","content":"...or how the wyrm has infected, afflicted and corrupted subtley them and their ways from the true path that was layed out for them...<br /> <br /> just as a thought<br /> <br /> Eventually for the Wyrm to be truly defeated maybe the Garou have to even wipe themselves clear and cleanse the world of even themselves so gaia has a chance.<br /> <br /> me... I like all the possibilities. Tells for great hope and equal despair in a World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T12:20:22-07:00","id":662103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=661786#post661786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's called 'Werewolf: the Apocalypse' and 'World of Darkness' for a reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>An Apocalypse is an unveiling, and darkness is just being in the unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 09-12-2015, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T16:16:20-07:00","id":662367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=661789#post661789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, they can't. They can try, but they'll end up destroying it. If they didn't have Rage, they would be able to. But they go have Rage. They will grow angry, furious beyond what humans can comprehend. They'll find irritation and insult in small things, because the big things that Rage is meant to be used for no longer exists. They'll frenzy, and destroy, and taste blood and flesh.<br /> <br /> They'll fulfil their purpose until the last Garou falls. No matter how hard they try, they can't help but to do otherwise. It's how Gaia designed them.<br /> <br /> They may have been intended to be an immune system, but Rage was their strength and their flaw, and they've long since become a cancer. Just ask the Fera, particularly the Grondr, or the Camaztotz. Ask the Bunyip, if you like.<br /> <br /> Part of the tragedy of the Garou is that increasingly more of them have realised this, and despite their best efforts they can't change who they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that's a cop out. The Garou did not do all their crap due to their Rage. They did all their crap because they were way too human. Their key issue isn't Rage or their Holy purpose, it's being human. And humans are dicks to other humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T03:24:05-07:00","id":662868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=662367#post662367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that's a cop out. The Garou did not do all their crap due to their Rage. They did all their crap because they were way too human. Their key issue isn't Rage or their Holy purpose, it's being human. And humans are dicks to other humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, 'they were way too human' is the cop out. It minimises the werewolf existence, negs on part of the core of their being to try and pretend they're not alien monsters.<br /> <br /> Sure, their similarity to humans makes them eminently capable of all the bad shit they did. But it's the worst parts of humanity amplified. It's a direct channel to Gaia's anger, and the rule book specifically states it's 'a force of mindless violence, a constant slow-motion path of unthinking destruction and violence that each and every Garou must keep control of lest it consume her'. Garou didn't just do all their bad shit because they were furry humans. They did their bad shit because they're furry humans with human-like foibles <i>and more violent, savage blood-lust and anger than any human will ever have</i>. Rage is as much a part of them as shapeshifting and Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Blaming their violent, irrevocable mistakes on simple humanity is the cop out. Taking humanity into account is fine. Ignoring the rest isn't.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T04:10:51-07:00","id":662902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=662103#post662103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Apocalypse is an unveiling, and darkness is just being in the unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> You may want to check y\u200bour dictionary, because an Apocalypse is most certainly not an unveiling, and your definition of darkness is wrong too, at least in context of &quot;The World of Darkness&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T04:52:04-07:00","id":662972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=662902#post662902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may want to check y\u200bour dictionary, because an Apocalypse is most certainly not an unveiling, and your definition of darkness is wrong too, at least in context of &quot;The World of Darkness&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the word originated from the Greek apokalypsis, meaning revelation, or to reveal.<br /> <br /> I agree that the more modern, destructive definition of the word is what is meant in the game's title, but I like the thought exercise of the Garou fighting against a great unveiling, even if it has no support in the game itself. Likewise, darkness meaning the unknown certainly fits the setting, but so does darkness meaning absence of light (since many of the setting's protagonists like functioning at night), or darkness meaning evil (we are playing monsters, after all).<br /> <br /> I don't disagree with Saur Ops Specialist that they can choose to interpret the titles to mean those definitions, but I don't think they're as supported by the setting as my earlier statement is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T06:50:56-07:00","id":663040,"title":"","content":"It can also mean a revelation, insight or unveiling of a catastrophic event.<br /> <br /> but we know what 'The Apocalypse' in terms of the game and setting refers too. The book was even put together and gave us multiple choices of an end should we of chosen to use it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think that as so many of us have so many different opinions and insights to the issues of the Garou as a whole (individuals might be alright <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> it's just when the pack, Sept, Tribal mentalities come in to play along with Camp, philosophical and differences in beliefs get in the way of true unity that it makes it difficult to make any true possible real difference...oh and politics of course.) That really the Garou Nation as a whole has more than any one problem or issue standing in their way.<br /> <br /> all of the above ideas and more could certainly be attributed to the shabby state they are in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T15:18:06-07:00","id":663513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=662868#post662868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, 'they were way too human' is the cop out. It minimises the werewolf existence, negs on part of the core of their being to try and pretend they're not alien monsters.<br /> <br /> Sure, their similarity to humans makes them eminently capable of all the bad shit they did. But it's the worst parts of humanity amplified. It's a direct channel to Gaia's anger, and the rule book specifically states it's 'a force of mindless violence, a constant slow-motion path of unthinking destruction and violence that each and every Garou must keep control of lest it consume her'. Garou didn't just do all their bad shit because they were furry humans. They did their bad shit because they're furry humans with human-like foibles <i>and more violent, savage blood-lust and anger than any human will ever have</i>. Rage is as much a part of them as shapeshifting and Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Blaming their violent, irrevocable mistakes on simple humanity is the cop out. Taking humanity into account is fine. Ignoring the rest isn't.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou are concious and sentient. They are fully in charge of their actions. Rage makes them testy and prone to horrifying outbursts, but it's their egoes and the justifications they make up for the crap that points out that their biggest problem is being human. For all the human mistakes they chide and seek to fix or eradicate, they do the same shit we have done to countless others through the centuries.<br /> <br /> They can control their Rage enough not to be genocidal maniacs. They choose not to. That is being human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T15:23:38-07:00","id":663515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=662367#post662367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that's a cop out. The Garou did not do all their crap due to their Rage. They did all their crap because they were way too human. Their key issue isn't Rage or their Holy purpose, it's being human. And humans are dicks to other humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the tribe that started the War of Tears and were the most vehement that the Bunyip needed to be exterminated right down to the last cub was the most <i>human</i> one? (Y'know, the Red Talons) Sorry. No sale. The werewolves do what they do because they are arrogant, violent, possess god-like power, and nobody can stop them. Not because they're human. If that assumption were even remotely true, humanity would have wiped itself from the face of the earth within a decade of the invention of the Atom Bomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T15:37:42-07:00","id":663520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=663515#post663515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the tribe that started the War of Tears and were the most vehement that the Bunyip needed to be exterminated right down to the last cub was the most <i>human</i> one? (Y'know, the Red Talons) Sorry. No sale. The werewolves do what they do because they are arrogant, violent, possess god-like power, and nobody can stop them. Not because they're human. If that assumption were even remotely true, humanity would have wiped itself from the face of the earth within a decade of the invention of the Atom Bomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd take a long hard look at all the attroctities we have done for power, religion, politics and simple pettiness through the ages before you conclude who is arrogant, violent and unwilling to stop for anyone. The wolf is simple and straightforward. It's not out there to murder everything and control it. That's the human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T23:13:53-07:00","id":663919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=663520#post663520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd take a long hard look at all the attroctities we have done for power, religion, politics and simple pettiness through the ages before you conclude who is arrogant, violent and unwilling to stop for anyone. The wolf is simple and straightforward. It's not out there to murder everything and control it. That's the human.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet... It wasn't the Glass Walkers that started the War of Tears and wiped out the Bunyip. Nor was it the Bone Gnawers... nor the Children of Gaia... If you were to rank the Garou from most-human to least, it's the<i> least</i>-human tribe that did that garbage. Do you see the Corax eradicating whole shapeshifter species? They're as human as the Garou. Have the Gurahl exterminated entire human cultures in a 3,000 year-long pogrom? They're as human as the Garou.<br /> <br /> Do humans to awful things? Sure. But I'd put it at better-than-even odds that nobody on my block is a mass-murderer. The same probably can't be said for the average sept.<br /> <br /> The werewolves do what they do because they are monsters. They can't say that the Devil-made-me-do-it. They are monsters because they <i>choose</i> to be. Being part-wolf or part-human has not a thing to do with it. To imply otherwise is to imply that an entirely human murderer (or rapist, or child-molester, or whatever) can simply shrug his shoulders and say &quot;It's not my fault. I'm human. It's just in my nature&quot; and escape all moral responsibility.<br /> <br /> It is <i>not</i> nature. It is <i>choice</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T00:01:44-07:00","id":663985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=663515#post663515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the tribe that started the War of Tears and were the most vehement that the Bunyip needed to be exterminated right down to the last cub was the most <i>human</i> one? (Y'know, the Red Talons) Sorry. No sale. The werewolves do what they do because they are arrogant, violent, possess god-like power, and nobody can stop them. Not because they're human. If that assumption were even remotely true, humanity would have wiped itself from the face of the earth within a decade of the invention of the Atom Bomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may have a point. I personally love wolves, and have done so since I was a kid, but I've heard of wolves that kill and eat other wolves moving into their territory or wolf cubs eating their own wounded parents while still alive. You hear stories about mice eating their young, or male cats killing kittens, so we may want to not knock humanity too hard. We aren't as savage as some other life forms at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T01:39:04-07:00","id":664046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=663919#post663919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The werewolves do what they do because they are monsters. They can't say that the Devil-made-me-do-it. They are monsters because they <i>choose</i> to be. Being part-wolf or part-human has not a thing to do with it. To imply otherwise is to imply that an entirely human murderer (or rapist, or child-molester, or whatever) can simply shrug his shoulders and say &quot;It's not my fault. I'm human. It's just in my nature&quot; and escape all moral responsibility.<br /> <br /> It is <i>not</i> nature. It is <i>choice</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why it's their human side that's to blame. It's not the Rage because Rage are point outbursts. It's not Gaia because she surely didn't make them for that. It's not the wolf because the wolf is the simple things in life. You come back to the human. And the human is the one thing that makes the Werwewolves the egoist bastards they are. The entitlement and the power tripping and the nature of being &quot;chosen&quot;. As for there being a choice, of course there is! That's the whole point of being human. We choose to do idiotic things, but the desire and capability of doing it stems from who we are and how we threat everything around us. My whole argument comes from Bunyip's claim that it's Rage that defines and explains why the Garou do horrible things and how they will end up killing Gaia.<br /> <br /> Even the Red Talons are actually infected with human ideas. For all their denial of their human side, they are still part man, and as prone to excesses as any other Garou. Heck their whole political movement for all its human hating has ideas that animals would never, ever consider, let alone implement.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T04:03:35-07:00","id":664085,"title":"","content":"No, my argument is that in the absence of everything else, Rage will still make the Garou do bad things. Rage is a weapon; while there are enemies to fight, it's a good weapon. In the absence of enemies, it's a self-consuming weapon. <br /> <br /> That goes beyond simple humanness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T13:33:55-07:00","id":664698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=664085#post664085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, my argument is that in the absence of everything else, Rage will still make the Garou do bad things. Rage is a weapon; while there are enemies to fight, it's a good weapon. In the absence of enemies, it's a self-consuming weapon.<br /> <br /> That goes beyond simple humanness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The absence of everything else isn't really a state that happens, though. Rage is stuck together with a conflicting opposite within the Garou and Fera, in addition to numerous other conflicting opposites. There's no true separation of human and beast for the Changers, and no true separation of Rage from the mentality you get from them. Everything is holistically wound-up inside of them, except for Ananasi and Nuwisha, who have different internal conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T10:25:10-07:00","id":665856,"title":"","content":"Just getting into the discussion at this point, but weren't the Red Talons tricked into starting to all out war against the super-secretive bunyip?<br /> Not sure how exactly, but it was a Black Spiral Dancer who made the Red Talon leader declare war, and that war was based on retribution, revenge and grief, right ?<br /> Emotions a wolf probably doesn't have, but than again, with the first-change lupus-born get a brain of a human - a human teenager that is.<br /> <br /> That said, the corax might not have on their own wiped out a entire race of changers, but their position in the war of rage is disputable and in the war of shame they were on the winning side, participating in the eradication if the panda changers. Okay, maybe not an entire race, but a tribe of another race, but still genocide.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Rage<br /> The mechanics regarding Rage are in my opinion stupid. First, revised edition started to make more used of &quot;The Beast&quot; as if rage and instincts were possessing the otherwise human garou. I find such formulations more suitable for vampire, but not garou. Instincts and rage should be integral parts of garou psyche. Secondly, the mechanics toward frenzy rolls seem somewhat unbalanced. I mean, difficulty 4 at full moon changes probability in a way that Frenzy becomes really common. Why in the world would that be the time to go to the holy place and meat with other garou to perform a moot rite, with something like the &quot;Breaking of the bones&quot; that will surely trigger frenzy rolls. And if one is triggered he endangers others, who's packmates get then frenzy rolls of them selves and we have what we LARPers call, Frenzy Domino. All tribes, except the Get of Fenris, who can raise the frenzy difficulty to 9 during gatherings via a rite, should stay at hope with the pack who is most likely not to trigger any frenzy rolls. Sure, the whole system is due to the Philodox is 6 and from there two steps to a full auspice means -2 difficulty. But in this way the whole rules don't support the setting, and that is just bad game design...as in &quot;one part of the game doesn't fit with another part, probably written by another author.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:16:44-07:00","id":665917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=665856#post665856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just getting into the discussion at this point, but weren't the Red Talons tricked into starting to all out war against the super-secretive bunyip?</div> </div> </div> </div>Writers and various W20 perspectives have been retconning the BSD influence out of this as a convenient excuse. The old story was that Wyrmbaiter's sister was killed by BSDs and made to look like the Bunyip did it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure how exactly, but it was a Black Spiral Dancer who made the Red Talon leader declare war, and that war was based on retribution, revenge and grief, right ?<br /> Emotions a wolf probably doesn't have, but than again, with the first-change lupus-born get a brain of a human - a human teenager that is. </div> </div> </div>Even saying probably as a rider is leaning close to &quot;are you a psychic?&quot; territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, the corax might not have on their own wiped out a entire race of changers, but their position in the war of rage is disputable and in the war of shame they were on the winning side, participating in the eradication if the panda changers. Okay, maybe not an entire race, but a tribe of another race, but still genocide. </div> </div> </div>Mostly as informants and spies, but the blood still clings, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> @Rage<br /> The mechanics regarding Rage are in my opinion stupid. First, revised edition started to make more used of &quot;The Beast&quot; as if rage and instincts were possessing the otherwise human garou. I find such formulations more suitable for vampire, but not garou. Instincts and rage should be integral parts of garou psyche. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, the mechanics toward frenzy rolls seem somewhat unbalanced. I mean, difficulty 4 at full moon changes probability in a way that Frenzy becomes really common. Why in the world would that be the time to go to the holy place and meat with other garou to perform a moot rite, with something like the &quot;Breaking of the bones&quot; that will surely trigger frenzy rolls. And if one is triggered he endangers others, who's packmates get then frenzy rolls of them selves and we have what we LARPers call, Frenzy Domino. All tribes, except the Get of Fenris, who can raise the frenzy difficulty to 9 during gatherings via a rite, should stay at hope with the pack who is most likely not to trigger any frenzy rolls. Sure, the whole system is due to the Philodox is 6 and from there two steps to a full auspice means -2 difficulty. But in this way the whole rules don't support the setting, and that is just bad game design...as in &quot;one part of the game doesn't fit with another part, probably written by another author.&quot; </div> </div> </div>WW was horrendously bad at math back in the day. Maybe that can also be reexamined in the hopeful W4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T16:17:52-07:00","id":666124,"title":"","content":"I would just assume that there is some crazy simple Moot Rite that puts a leash on the Rage as long as you are in a Caern where everyone is gathered for the purpose of communing with Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-15-2015, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T21:18:53-07:00","id":666435,"title":"","content":"I have to tag in here and join the death-and-desolation camp. Gaia gave the Garou Rage, but the Wyrm corrupted it. It's not the humanity of the Garou that provokes them to atrocities, it's the Wyrm. That's a key point of what Werewolf: The Apocalypse. The Horror you fight with Rage and tooth and claw until you're laying bloody on the ground beside your kin... that horror is deep inside of you. And you're it's instrument every bit as much as you are it's enemy.<br /> The Garou can't win, because at the end of the day the evil is inside them. If the Garou beat back the Wyrm, it would still be in their hearts. I think this would create a depressingly poetic Apocalypse. The Garou find a way to beat back the existential horror of the Wyrm, celebrate their victory, begin building the world they desire.. Only to see it all ruined and brought to a tragic, end as Gaia's lifeblood stains the Garou's hands from the atrocities the victorious Garou Nation first inflicts on the world and then on each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7861-strafe","name":"Strafe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T22:49:08-07:00","id":666483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=666435#post666435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to tag in here and join the death-and-desolation camp. Gaia gave the Garou Rage, but the Wyrm corrupted it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't how it works, and if you go down that path you might as well just rip out the comic in the front of W20 with the Eighth Sign of the Phoenix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T23:13:01-07:00","id":666490,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Let us remember how much the Garou values Honor and Wisdom. It's not that of all the creatures in the world they aren't uniquely disposed to screwing up. They are. But so are humans. The question is, as with humans, can they gain the necessary self knowledge that will allow themselves to compensate for their negative predispositions and be able to successfully set up a culture that will be able to continuously hand down this wisdom to a new generation, or are they doomed to not only be dragged down by their flaws but take the world down with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:02:04-07:00","id":667267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=666435#post666435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to tag in here and join the death-and-desolation camp. Gaia gave the Garou Rage, but the Wyrm corrupted it. It's not the humanity of the Garou that provokes them to atrocities, it's the Wyrm. That's a key point of what Werewolf: The Apocalypse. The Horror you fight with Rage and tooth and claw until you're laying bloody on the ground beside your kin... that horror is deep inside of you. And you're it's instrument every bit as much as you are it's enemy.<br /> The Garou can't win, because at the end of the day the evil is inside them. If the Garou beat back the Wyrm, it would still be in their hearts. I think this would create a depressingly poetic Apocalypse. The Garou find a way to beat back the existential horror of the Wyrm, celebrate their victory, begin building the world they desire.. Only to see it all ruined and brought to a tragic, end as Gaia's lifeblood stains the Garou's hands from the atrocities the victorious Garou Nation first inflicts on the world and then on each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a tale of personal and world horror. I really like this as an intro and of the internal battle waged against the seeds of doubt that could plague a gaian warriors mind after all the horrors and blasphemies they've witnessed. The umbral realms battling the wyrm at all sides, malfeas and the atrocity realms reminding that bad things not only stay and stick around some place but they actually feed the enemy as their memories of the acts of billions over centuries of war, hate, abuse and destruction live on more potently than heroic legends of the Garou.<br /> <br /> It's too much, the weight of it is too much bear, there isnt enough time, there arent enough garou let alone enough to trust and work together...then the Harano kicks in.<br /> <br /> 'it'll never be enough time<br /> <br /> They'll always be something. Even if it's ourselves that are the problem... '<br /> <br /> I like it. Of course there's nothing to say individuals wont be inspired to work harder or even have some success...maybe even save the world in our own games. But that doesnt mean everyone has to see it and follow it the same as anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T12:22:45-07:00","id":667348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=666483#post666483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't how it works...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it might very well <i>be</i> how it works. One of the tertiary plots in W:tA is that the Theurges have a recurring debate from time to time about the spiritual nature of Rage itself. Most Garou (for obvious reasons) hold that Rage was a gift from Luna. Some Theurges however (and heretically in the minds of many Garou) posit that it is in fact a curse of the Wyrm and has nothing to do with Luna at all. A somewhat larger minority (and still somewhat heretically in the minds of many Garou) maintain that it <i>was</i> a gift from Luna, but through their own sins, the Garou unintentionally allowed the Wyrm into the collective soul of the Garou and thereby allowed this great gift to be cursed by the Wyrm -- and this is why the Garou in the modern age have so little control over their Rage and why there <i>is</i> such a thing as Thrall-of-the-Wyrm frenzies. Incidentally, this basic concept was a fairly central plot element in Last Battle (although that novel was never officially canon).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 09-16-2015, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T13:40:35-07:00","id":667395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=667348#post667348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it might very well <i>be</i> how it works. One of the tertiary plots in W:tA is that the Theurges have a recurring debate from time to time about the spiritual natuncidentallre of Rage itself. Most Garou (for obvious reasons) hold that Rage was a gift from Luna. Some Theurges however (and heretically in the minds of many Garou) posit that it is in fact a curse of the Wyrm and has nothing to do with Luna at all. A somewhat larger minority (and still somewhat heretically in the minds of many Garou) maintain that it <i>was</i> a gift from Luna, but through their own sins, the Garou unintentionally allowed the Wyrm into the collective soul of the Garou and thereby allowed this great gift to be cursed by the Wyrm -- and this is why the Garou in the modern age have so little control over their Rage and why there <i>is</i> such a thing as Thrall-of-the-Wyrm frenzies. Incidentally, this basic concept was a fairly central plot element in Last Battle (although that novel was never officially canon).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thus by default, it isn't how it works, and if the thing is to be debated in-setting, they shouldn't have ever called them Thrall of the Wyrm frenzies as a system term (in 1e, they didn't even exist). The consequences of the Garou's actions are better off being standing on their own without the &quot;we have sinned and are cursed&quot; aspects that edge closer to Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T20:05:10-07:00","id":667739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=664046#post664046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's why it's their human side that's to blame. It's not the Rage because Rage are point outbursts. It's not Gaia because she surely didn't make them for that. It's not the wolf because the wolf is the simple things in life. You come back to the human. And the human is the one thing that makes the Werwewolves the egoist bastards they are. The entitlement and the power tripping and the nature of being &quot;chosen&quot;. As for there being a choice, of course there is! That's the whole point of being human. We choose to do idiotic things, but the desire and capability of doing it stems from who we are and how we threat everything around us. My whole argument comes from Bunyip's claim that it's Rage that defines and explains why the Garou do horrible things and how they will end up killing Gaia.<br /> <br /> Even the Red Talons are actually infected with human ideas. For all their denial of their human side, they are still part man, and as prone to excesses as any other Garou. Heck their whole political movement for all its human hating has ideas that animals would never, ever consider, let alone implement.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've never cared for this misanthropic view. And honestly, some of the WtA product line is responsible for it. But I think there's a few points here. Humans aren't inherently evil, and it's not the &quot;human side&quot; of a Garou, if such a thing can be said to exist, that makes the Garou worse. Humans are of Gaia. Left the way Gaia had created them, Humans would have existed within the Balance and not pursued the excesses that are killing Gaia today.<br /> The Garou are their own downfall, for the same reason that humanity is so flawed. The Wyrm. The Wyrm corrupts all things of Gaia. It's the corruption of the Wyrm that makes humans as bad as they are in the World of Darkness. And it's the Wyrm's taint on the Garou that caused the Impergium and the War of Rage and the inter-tribal fighting. It's the Wyrm's touch that takes Rage from being a pure force for the defense of Gaia and twists it into an instrument of self-harm.<br /> I feel that this inner-corruption of the Garou is absolutely essential for the horror of WtA to come through. A Garou is the monster he fights. Garou are heroes, but not simple ones. They're monsters, and they commit innumerable crimes of their own. They're tragic heroes that ruin their own cause. And this is critical. Because without this inner-corruption, I feel you depart from the themes of WtA into a Furry-Gritty-Captain Planet game instead.<br /> And that's why in my view, a Garou victory would have to end in self-defeat. Anything less than that misses the entire point. Of course, your Chronicle may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7861-strafe","name":"Strafe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T00:41:19-07:00","id":667949,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm pushes, but we're the ones that choose to listen. The Wyrm does not have a foothold where depravity, wickedness,selfishness and greed don't fester themselves. We're special among Gaia's children that we have created so much and managed to be so glorious in our achievements, yet we are unable to live and let live. That's the human condition, and while in the context of Werewolf it's easy to forget, humanity is capable for glorious deeds as much as they are capable for horrors. Getting the Garou to go beyond their comfort zone and to actually tap the capacity of humans for good may be the only way to actually alleviate or even prevent the Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T02:14:56-07:00","id":668015,"title":"","content":"wasn't there already a time in the past when Garou 'won'? As far as I remember it ended up with twar with Fera and destruction of several changing breeds. Add to that all the annesessary violence they engage in despite being on the edge of extinction. Yeah, letting religious zealots, with extreme anger issues, rule the world is not a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:19:53-07:00","id":668211,"title":"","content":"There wasn't. Even back then the Wyrm was strong and a force to be reckoned with (which is not the theoretical post Wyrm utopia the OP is talking about). Also, it's not about ruling the world, it's about what happens when there are no more obvious enemies to fight. Nota bene, I find the whole concept preposterous. Eliminating all bad shit in the world, fighting every monster that ever existed or will exist, changing the nature of a principal force of existence and fixing the dying body of the Goddess are all things is not something that will ever leave the setting recognizable in any way, shape or form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:09:24-07:00","id":668494,"title":"","content":"It would be an entirely different type of existence as we as forms would know.<br /> <br /> but there's no reason someone couldnt try to create and play such an idea if that is what appeals to them as players. Imagination is the only limitation for roleplaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:10:27-07:00","id":668730,"title":"","content":"I feel with that the wolves would give rise to another urge wyrm of fear. We're assuming here that the wyrm can be destroyed in the first place. I'm not so certain. I'm also a fan of the cyclical time idea though (I.e. The apocalypse isn't the apocalypse but more of a reset). The only way the garou can truly win is if they go themselves, or their wyrm natures will just give birth to another bane to take its place, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:19:43-07:00","id":668736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=668730#post668730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel with that the wolves would give rise to another urge wyrm of fear. We're assuming here that the wyrm can be destroyed in the first place. I'm not so certain. I'm also a fan of the cyclical time idea though (I.e. The apocalypse isn't the apocalypse but more of a reset). The only way the garou can truly win is if they go themselves, or their wyrm natures will just give birth to another bane to take its place, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>OP only mentioned managing to kill Pentex and the BSDs, so in this case the &quot;victory&quot; is more like a reprieve from most of the current threats. Also, given how important Pentex's subsidiaries were, there would be, at minimum, a global depression.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;their Wyrm natures&quot;, again, it doesn't really work like that except for particular games. Much like tribal weaknesses, playing connect the dots with triatic Wyrms and breeds isn't something integral to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:23:45-07:00","id":668745,"title":"","content":"No, but rage, depression and other issues (shadow lord ambition) would breed the issue back. <br /> <br /> Honestly a global depression would be a boon and grief to the cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T19:53:56-07:00","id":669150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=668736#post668736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for &quot;their Wyrm natures&quot;, again, it doesn't really work like that except for particular games. Much like tribal weaknesses, playing connect the dots with triatic Wyrms and breeds isn't something integral to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The corruption of the Garou and their self-imposed doom is, I think, a significant theme to WtA, though. It's not that the Garou have a &quot;Wyrm nature.&quot; It's that the Wyrm corrupts the things of Gaia. All of them. The Garou are explicitly not exempt to this. That's the insidious horror of WtA. Not all the Wyrm's corruption is as obvious as the Dancers or Fomori. The haunting terror of the Wyrm is the subtle, gradual corruption of the souls of even Gaia's greatest defenders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7861-strafe","name":"Strafe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T22:13:53-07:00","id":669251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=669150#post669150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The corruption of the Garou and their self-imposed doom is, I think, a significant theme to WtA, though. It's not that the Garou have a &quot;Wyrm nature.&quot; It's that the Wyrm corrupts the things of Gaia. All of them. The Garou are explicitly not exempt to this. That's the insidious horror of WtA. Not all the Wyrm's corruption is as obvious as the Dancers or Fomori. The haunting terror of the Wyrm is the subtle, gradual corruption of the souls of even Gaia's greatest defenders.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are mistakes, follies, and terrible wrongs which the Wyrm does not, and perhaps cannot, use to corrupt. When it takes advantage of the harsh purity of its opposition, its tendrils can trick, but not corrode or make the thing its own. This is the state of the Garou; their purpose has led them to do terrible things, and their enemies have taken advantage of these time and again, but never have the Garou fallen from grace. They were meant to be crude and bellicose, and that makes horror stick around even if the Wyrm were to sit down and act nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T03:45:14-07:00","id":669445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/656711-what-would-a-victorious-garou-nation-look-like?p=669251#post669251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are mistakes, follies, and terrible wrongs which the Wyrm does not, and perhaps cannot, use to corrupt. When it takes advantage of the harsh purity of its opposition, its tendrils can trick, but not corrode or make the thing its own. This is the state of the Garou; their purpose has led them to do terrible things, and their enemies have taken advantage of these time and again, but never have the Garou fallen from grace. They were meant to be crude and bellicose, and that makes horror stick around even if the Wyrm were to sit down and act nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I so wish I could play Werewolf with you, Dino.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}